    "updated_at": "2020-09-20T21:45:02Z",
    "body": "One bad thing in this mess is that if I explicitly enable a py2 virtualenv/conda env, then this won't show up anymore, but still the system py3 one. At least all my virtualenvs (currently py3 ones) have a `bin/python` which links to a py3 binary (they all also have a `bin/python3` so setting to python3 works for python v3). \r\n\r\nMaybe this is an argument to first check for `python` and only if that does't exist, for `python3`?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
