    "updated_at": "2020-10-03T09:57:53Z",
    "body": "Something else we should think about is what is the expected case with venvs that are in a given directory but might not have been activated as mentioned in #1529. Should Starship try to detect if there is a virtualenv in the current directory and if there is try to work out what version it is using? The only thing I'm worried about is that this could get complicated since the venv could be created multiple ways e.g just calling the `venv` module, pipenv or poetry each of which will have their own complications.\r\n\r\n@romabysen  and @Tadaboody you have both been involved with the other issue what do you think?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
